From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 13:15:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] [VideoRenderers] Resolve overlay geometry for the whole
 frame before drawing

CRenderer::Render walked the overlay buffer and drew each overlay as it went,
so nothing in the renderer could ever see more than one overlay at a time. That
is enough while every overlay is placed purely from its own coordinates, and
not enough for anything that has to reason about what else is on screen.

Split the geometry out of the drawing. Render(COverlay*) becomes
GetRenderState(COverlay*, SRenderState&), which fills in the placement and
stops there. Render(int) and RenderHDROverlays collect the whole frame as
SRenderItems first, through ResolveRenderItems, and draw them afterwards.
CDebugRenderer, the only other caller, resolves and draws in the same two
steps.

Two things the libass branch of PrepareOverlays was doing for itself move out
of the loop, because they are not libass specific:

  - loading the subtitle settings and rebuilding the style, which previously
    never ran at all on a stream carrying no libass track, leaving the cached
    subtitle position and vertical margin at zero;
  - reconciling the subtitle position with the resolution info, now
    SyncSubtitlePosition, which also writes back a position the user changed
    during playback.

Both now run once per frame for any overlay. Note updateStyle is consequently
true for every libass overlay in the frame it changes on, where before only the
first one saw it - m_isSettingsChanged was cleared by the first element to look
at it. That is the more correct of the two behaviours.

No functional change.

